Production of Polymers, BREF POL (@ic-polymers: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_01PXATYT6P16206KQ3VDX34K1F
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Production of Polymers, BREF POL. adopted August 2007. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/production-polymers).

The book addresses selected industrial polymer and rubber families, their process operations, infrastructure, losses/recovery and environmental evidence. Coverage is explicitly selected rather than exhaustive for every polymer.

Read the complete generic production/operation material and whole relevant family chapters. Connect monomer/initiator/catalyst chemistry, distributions, heat/removal, phases, finishing, residual monomer and product use. The full relevant process study deepens the industrial chemistry; detailed polymer science and materials production retain their specialist scope.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled. The official full PDF has 314 file pages.

